              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ventilō, ventilāre — \"to winnow; to fan, to toss in the air\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Agricolae frūmentum in āreā ventilant. The farmers winnow the grain on the threshing floor."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ventilō, ventilāre, ventilāvī, ventilātum. English ventilate comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
