          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "stipula is inherited from Proto-Italic stipelā 'straw' (EtymDB), and Lewis & Short connect it with stīpes 'stake, trunk'. English stubble comes, through French, from a related Late Latin form."
            }
          ]
        },
